          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            %em F-theory
            is a toolbox for describing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIB+string+theory"} type IIB string theory
            backgrounds –
            %em including
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+effects"} non-perturbative effects
            induced from the presence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D7-branes"} D7-branes
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28p%2Cq%29-strings"} (p,q)-strings
            – in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibrations"} elliptic fibrations
            whose fiber modulus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi τ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
            encodes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axio-dilaton"} axio-dilaton
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+coupling+constant"} string coupling constant
            and the degree-0
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL(2, \mathbb{Z})
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U-duality"} U-duality
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} duality in string theory
          %p
            More technically, F-theory is what results when
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactifying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptic fibration
            (which yields
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+superstring+theory"} type IIA superstring theory
            compactified on a
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundle"} fiber bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
            with respect to one of the two cycles of the elliptic fiber. The result is (uncompactified)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIB+superstring+theory"} type IIB superstring theory
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axio-dilaton"} axio-dilaton
            given by the moduli of the original elliptic fibration, see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#From11dSupergravity"} below
          %p
            Or rather, this is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIB+string+theory"} type IIB string theory
            with some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+effects"} non-perturbative effects
            included, reducing to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+string+theory"} perturbative string theory
            in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sen+limit"} Sen limit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            available also F-theory should be a full non-perturbative description of type IIB string theory, but absent that it is some kind of approximation. For instance while the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+group"} modular
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+group"} structure group
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptic fibration
            in principle encodes (necessarily non-perturbative)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
            effects, it is presently not actually known in full detail how this affects the full theory, notably the proper charge quantization law of the 3-form fluxes, see at
            %em
              %a{:href => "S-duality#CohomologicalNatureOfTypeIIFieldsUnderSDuality"} S-duality – Cohomological nature of the fields under S-duality
            for more on that.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#From11dSupergravity Relation to M-theory
          %p
            The
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+M-theory+and+F-theory"} duality between M-theory and F-theory
          %p
            The following line of argument shows why first compactifying M-theory on a torus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                    %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %msubsup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                    %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_1^A \times S_1^B
            to get type IIA on a circle and then T-dualizing that circle to get type IIB indeed only depends on the shape
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{R_A}{R_B}
            of the torus, but not on its other geometry.
          %p
            By the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualities+in+string+theory"} dualities in string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string theory
            is supposed to be obtained from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/UV-completion"} UV-completion
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            by first
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+mechanism"} dimensionally reducing
            over a circle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi S
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1_A
            – to obtain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+supergravity"} type IIA supergravity
            – and then applying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
            along another circle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi S
                    %mi B
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1_B
            to obtain
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIB+supergravity"} type IIB supergravity
          %p
            To obtain type IIB sugra in noncompact 10 dimensions this way, also
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi S
                    %mi B
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1_B
            is to be compactified (since
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
            sends the radius
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_A
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi S
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1_A
            to the inverse radius
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mi B
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi s
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_B = \ell_s^2 / R_A
            of
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi S
                      %mi B
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1_B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %mn 10
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 10
            is obtained from 11d sugra compactified on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torus"} torus
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi S
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %msubsup
                      %mi S
                      %mi B
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1_A \times S^1_B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
            and this may vary over the 9d base space as an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptic fibration
          %p
            Applying T-duality to one of the compact direction yields a 10-dimensional theory which may now be thought of as encoded by a 12-dimensional elliptic fibration. This 12d elliptic fibration encoding a 10d type II supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum"} vacuum
            is the input data that F-theory is concerned with.
          %p A schematic depiction of this story is the following:
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
                %th
                %th
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11d+supergravity"} M-theory
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo =
                        %mn 11
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 11
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  F-theory in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo =
                        %mn 12
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 12
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \downarrow
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+mechanism"} KK-reduction
                  along
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptic fibration
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \downarrow
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axio-dilaton"} axio-dilaton
                  is modulus of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptic fibration
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"} IIA string theory
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo =
                        %mn 9
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 9
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ←
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leftarrow
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo →
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rightarrow
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIB+string+theory"} IIB string theory
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo =
                        %mn 10
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 10
          %p
            In the simple case where the elliptic fiber is indeed just
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi S
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %msubsup
                      %mi S
                      %mi B
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1_A \times S^1_B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/imaginary+part"} imaginary part
            of its complex modulus is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Im
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Im(\tau) = \frac{R_A}{R_B}
                  \\,.
          %p
            By following through the above diagram, one finds how this determines the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coupling+constant"} coupling constant
            in the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string theory
          %p
            First, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi S
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1_A
            yields a type IIA
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+coupling"} string coupling
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mi IIA
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℓ
                        %mi s
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g_{IIA} = \frac{R_A}{\ell_s}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Then the T-duality operation along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi S
                    %mi B
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1_B
            divides this by
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_B
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mi IIB
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mi IIA
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi ℓ
                                %mi s
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi R
                                %mi B
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi R
                                %mi A
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi R
                                %mi B
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi Im
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi τ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  g_{IIB} &amp; = g_{IIA} \frac{\ell_s}{R_B}
                  \\\
                  \&amp; = \frac{R_A}{R_B}
                  \\\
                  \&amp; = Im(\tau)
                  \\end{aligned}
                  \\,.
          %h4#relation_to_mtheory_on_manifolds
            Relation to M-theory on
            = succeed "-manifolds" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
          %p
            In order to get minimal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N%3D1+d%3D4+supergravity"} N=1 d=4 supergravity
            after
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+G%E2%82%82-manifolds"} M-theory on G₂-manifolds
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory+on+CY4-manifolds"} F-theory on CY4-manifolds
          %p
            Discussion of the relation between then
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82-manifold"} G₂-manifold
            fibers for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+G%E2%82%82-manifolds"} M-theory on G₂-manifolds
            and the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calabi-Yau+manifold"} Calabi-Yau 4-manifold
            fibers in F-theory includes (
            %a{:href => "#GukovYauZaslow02"}> Gukov-Yau-Zaslow 02
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Belhaj02"} Belhaj 02
          %h4#relation_to_heterotic_mtheory_on_adesingularities Relation to heterotic M-theory on ADE-singularities
          %p
            Relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+M-theory+on+ADE-singularities"} heterotic M-theory on ADE-singularities
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Monika+Marquart"}> Monika Marquart
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Waldram"} Daniel Waldram
                %em
                  F-theory duals of M-theory on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ×
                        %msup
                          %mi T
                          %mn 4
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1/\mathbb{Z}_2 \times T^4 / \mathbb{Z}_N
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0204228"}> arXiv:hep-th/0204228
                )
            %li
              %p
                Christoph Lüdeling,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fabian+Ruehle"} Fabian Ruehle
                = succeed "," do
                  %em F-theory duals of singular heterotic K3 models
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1405.2928"} arXiv:1405.2928
          %h3#RelationToOrientifolds Relation to orientifold type II backgrounds
          %p
            The general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum"} vacuum
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+superstring+theory"} type II superstring theory
            (including
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+I+superstring+theory"} type I superstring theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifold"} orientifold
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            data of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifold"} orientifold
            is a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+system"} local system
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+stack"} smooth stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptic fibration
            that defines the F-theory is a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi SL
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL_2(\mathbb{Z})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+system"} local system
            (being the “homological invariant” of the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptic fibration
          %p
            An argument due to (
            %a{:href => "#Sen96"}> Sen 96
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Sen97a"} Sen 97a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifold"} orientifold
            data along the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            inclusion
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi SL
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2 \hookrightarrow SL_2(\mathbb{Z})
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sen+limit"} Sen limit
          %p
            The degeneration locus of the elliptic fibration – where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discriminant"} discriminant
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            vanishes and its fibers are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nodal+curve"} nodal curve
            – is interpreted as that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D7-branes"} D7-branes
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/O-planes"} O7-planes
            (
            %a{:href => "#Sen97a"}> Sen 97a, (3)
            ,
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#Blumenhagen10"} Blumenhagen 10, (11)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+enhancement"} gauge enhancement
            %a{:href => "#Sen97b"} Sen 97b
            see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#SingularLocusAndD7Branes"} below
          %p
            Reasoning like this might suggest that in generalization to how type II
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifolds"} orientifolds
            involve
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant"} equivariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            (namely
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KR-theory"} KR-theory
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi SL
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL_2(\mathbb{Z})
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology"} elliptic cohomology
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#KrizSati05"} Kriz-Sati 05, p. 3, p.17, 18
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+equivariant+elliptic+cohomology"} modular equivariant elliptic cohomology
          %h3#relation_to_heterotic_string_theory Relation to heterotic string theory
          %p
            The
            = succeed ":A" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+F-theory+and+heterotic+string+theory"} duality between F-theory and heterotic string theory
          %p
            F-theory on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptically fibered
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3"} K3
            is supposed to be equivalent to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} compactified
            on a 2-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torus"}> torus
            \. An early argument for this is due to (
            %a{:href => "#Sen96"}> Sen 96
            ).
          %p
            More generally, heterotic string theory on an elliptically fibered Calabi-Yau
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z \to B
            of complex dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            is supposed to be equivalent
            = succeed "-theory" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to B
            with elliptic K3-fibers.
          %p
            A detailed discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            of the respective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+spaces"} moduli spaces
            is originally due to (
            %a{:href => "#FriedmanMorganWitten97"}> Friedman-Morgan-Witten 97
            ). A review of this is in (
            %a{:href => "#Donagi98"}> Donagi 98
            ).
          %h3#SingularLocusAndD7Branes Singular locus of the elliptic fibration and D7-branes
          %p
            In passing from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"} type IIA string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+monopole"} Kaluza-Klein monopole
            in 11d becomes the locus of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
            in 10d. The locus of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+monopole"} Kaluza-Klein monopole
            in turn (as discussed there) is the locus where the
            = succeed "-circle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi S
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1_A
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi S
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %msubsup
                      %mi S
                      %mi B
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1_A \times S^1_B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptic fibration
            degenerates to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nodal+curve"} nodal curve
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-dual
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
            are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D7-branes"} D7-branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D7-branes"} D7-branes
            in F-theory “are” the singular locus of the elliptic fibration.
          %p
            Now an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptically+fibered+complex+K3-surface"} elliptically fibered complex K3-surface
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi K
                          %mn 3
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℂ
                          %msup
                            %mi ℙ
                            %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  T &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; K3
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbb{C}\mathbb{P}^1
                  }
          %p
            may be parameterized via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weierstrass+elliptic+function"} Weierstrass elliptic function
            as the solution locus of the equation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi y
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 3
                  %mo +
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  y^2 = x^3 + f(z) x + g(z)
          %p
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi ℙ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y,z \in \mathbb{C}\mathbb{P}^1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial"} polynomial
            of degree 8 and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            of degree twelve. The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/j-invariant"} j-invariant
            of the complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
            which this parameterizes for given
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mn 4
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 24
                      %mi f
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mn 3
                    %mrow
                      %mn 27
                      %msup
                        %mi g
                        %mn 2
                      %mo +
                      %mn 4
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mn 3
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  j(\tau(z)) = \frac{4 (24 f)^3}{27 g^2 + 4 f^3}
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poles"} poles
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo →
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j\to \infty
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/j-invariant"} j-invariant
            correspond to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nodal+curve"} nodal curve
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D7-branes"} D7-branes
            are located.
          .float_right_image{:style => "margin: -40px 0px 20px 20px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:alt => "homotopy pasting diagram exhibiting the homotopy Whitehead integral", :src => "/nlab/files/K3CobordismBetween24ThreeSpheres.jpg", :width => "260px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                from
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/Equivariant+Cohomotopy+and+Oriented+Cohomology+Theory"} SS21
          %p
            Since the order of the poles is 24 (the polynomial degree of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discriminant"} discriminant
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo =
                    %mn 27
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %mn 4
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta = 27 g^2 + 4 f^3
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptically+fibered+K3-surface"} elliptically fibered K3-surface
                –
                %a{:href => "elliptic+fibration+of+a+K3-surface#SingularPoints"} singular points
            %em 24 D7-branes
            (
            %a{:href => "#Sen96"}> Sen 96, page 5
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Sen97b"} Sen 97b
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Morrison04"} Morrison 04, sections 8 and 17
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Denef08"} Denef 08, around (3.41)
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "duality+between+M%2FF-theory+and+heterotic+string+theory#DouglasParkSchnell14"} Douglas-Park-Schnell 14
          %p
            Under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
            this translates to 24
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"} type IIA string theory
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3"} K3
            (
            %a{:href => "#Vafa96"}> Vafa 96, Footnote 2 on p. 6
            ).
          %p
            Notice that the
            %em net charge
            of these 24 D7-branes is supposed to vanish, due to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
            effects (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Denef08"} Denef 08, below (3.41)
          %p
            For analogous discussion of 24 NS5-branes in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3"} K3
            see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "duality+in+string+theory#Schwarz97"} Schwarz 97, around p. 50
          %p
            For more see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/24+branes+transverse+to+K3"} 24 branes transverse to K3
          %h3#Fbranescan F-brane scan
          %div
            %p
              %strong
                from
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-branes"} M-branes
                to F-branes:
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstrings"} superstrings
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-branes"} NS5-branes
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th
                    %strong
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
                    on
                    = succeed "-" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msubsup
                              %mi S
                              %mi A
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ×
                            %msubsup
                              %mi S
                              %mi B
                              %mn 1
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1_A \times S^1_B
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptic fibration
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
                    on
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi S
                            %mi A
                            %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1_A
                  %th
                    %strong
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"} type IIA string theory
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-dual
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
                    on
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi S
                            %mi B
                            %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1_B
