                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E6"}> E6
                    \-,
                    = succeed "-," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E7"} E7
                    = succeed "-" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E8"} E8
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+enhancement"} gauge enhancement
            %p
              (e.g.
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "F-theory#Johnson97"} Johnson 97
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "F-theory#Blumenhagen10"} Blumenhagen 10
          %h3#sduality_operation_on_branes
            S-duality operation on
            = succeed "-branes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p,q)
          %p
            The F-theory picture gives a geometric interpretation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
            expected in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string theory
            %em two
            integer charges
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi p
                  %mo ,
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p,q)
            acted on by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL(2,\mathbb{Z})
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F1-brane"} F1-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D1-brane"} D1-brane
            combine to the
            = succeed "-string," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p,q)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-brane"} NS5-brane
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D5-brane"} D5-brane
            combine to a
            = succeed "-5-brane." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p,q)
          %p
            Namely in the F-theory picture this comes from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wrapped+brane"} wrapping
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            and the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-dualizing
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Johnson97"} Johnson 97, p. 4
          %h3#ModelBuildingAndPhenomenology Model building and phenomenology
          %p
            For F-theory a fairly advanced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28physics%29"} model
            building and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+phenomenology"} string phenomenology
            has been developed. A detailed review is in (
            %a{:href => "#Denef08"}> Denef 08
            ).
          %p
            Via the relation between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry+and+Calabi-Yau+manifolds"} supersymmetry and Calabi-Yau manifolds
            there is particular interest in F-theory compactified on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calabi-Yau+variety"} Calabi-Yau spaces
            of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"}> complex
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            4. For more on this see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F%2FM-theory+on+elliptically+fibered+Calabi-Yau+4-folds"} F/M-theory on elliptically fibered Calabi-Yau 4-folds
          %p
            A large number of realizations of the exact field content of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            (or rather the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSSM"} MSSM
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#CveticHalversonLinLiuTian19"} Cvetic-Halverson-Lin-Liu-Tian 19
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F%27-theory"} F'-theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D12+supergravity"}> D=12 supergravity
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D14+supersymmetry"} D=14 supersymmetry
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+M-theory"} bosonic M-theory
          %div
            %p
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactified
                on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptically fibered
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+analytic+space"} complex analytic
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundle"} fiber
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi dim
                            %mi ℂ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Σ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dim_{\mathbb{C}}(\Sigma)
                  %th 1
                  %th 2
                  %th 3
                  %th 4
                  %th 5
              %tbody
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F%2FM-theory+on+elliptically+fibered+Calabi-Yau+2-folds"} F-theory on CY2
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F%2FM-theory+on+elliptically+fibered+Calabi-Yau+3-folds"} F-theory on CY3
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F%2FM-theory+on+elliptically+fibered+Calabi-Yau+4-folds"} F-theory on CY4
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F%2FM-theory+on+elliptically+fibered+Calabi-Yau+5-folds"} F-theory on CY5
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory+on+Spin%287%29-manifolds"} F-theory on Spin(7)-manifolds
          %h2#References References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
            in the strong coupling limit is due to
          %ul
            %li#Schwarz96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"}> John Schwarz
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em M Theory Extensions of T Duality
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Frontiers in Quantum Field Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9601077"} arXiv:hep-th/9601077
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/3245"} doi:10.1142/3245
            %li#Russo97
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jorge+Russo"}> Jorge Russo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em T-duality in M-theory and supermembranes
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9701188"} arXiv:hep-th/9701188
          %p
            That
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string theory
            may be interpreted in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+transformations"} conformal transformations
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            compactified on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torus"} torus
            was originally observed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"}> John Schwarz
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    An
                    = succeed "-Multiplet" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi SL
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 2
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL(2,\mathbb{Z})
                %strong 360
                (1995) 13-18 ERRATUM-ibid. B
                %strong 364
                (1995) 252 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9508143"}> arXiv:hep-th/9508143
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Aspinwall"}> Paul Aspinwall
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Some Relationships Between Dualities in String Theory
                %strong 46
                (1996) 30-38 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9508154"}> arXiv:hep-th/9508154
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0920-5632(96)00004-7"} doi:10.1016/0920-5632(96)00004-7
          %p The original article on F-theory as such is
          %ul
            %li#Vafa96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"}> Cumrun Vafa
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Evidence for F-theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9602022"} arXiv:hep-th/9602022
          %p
            An early survey of its relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Johnson97
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+Johnson"}> Clifford Johnson
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em From M-theory to F-theory, with Branes
              %strong 507
              (1997) 227-244 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9706155"}> arXiv:hep-th/9706155
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0550-3213(97)00550-6"} doi:10.1016/S0550-3213(97)00550-6
          %p A more recent survey is
          %ul
            %li#Blumenhagen10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralph+Blumenhagen"}> Ralph Blumenhagen
              ,
              %em Basics of F-theory from the Type IIB Perspective
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1002.2836"}> arXiv:1002.2836
              )
          %p Lecture notes include
          %ul
            %li#Morrison04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Morrison"}> David Morrison
                ,
                %em TASI Lectures on Compactification and Duality
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0411120"}> arXiv:hep-th/0411120
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Timo+Weigand"}> Timo Weigand
                ,
                %em Lectures on F-theory compactifications and model building
                Class. Quantum Grav. 27 214004 (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1009.3497"}> arXiv:1009.3497
                )
            %li#Weigand18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Timo+Weigand"}> Timo Weigand
                ,
                %em TASI Lectures on F-theory
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.01854"}> arXiv:1806.01854
                )
          %p Textbook accounts include
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Katrin+Becker"}> Katrin Becker
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Melanie+Becker"} Melanie Becker
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"} John Schwarz
              = succeed "," do
                %em String Theory and M-Theory: A Modern Introduction
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511816086"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511816086
          %p Further survey:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Timo+Weigand"}> Timo Weigand
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em F-theory: Progress and Prospects
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.theorie.physik.uni-muenchen.de/activities/workshops/archive_workshops_conferences/string_pheno_ringberg/slides_frontiers/weigand.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Vafa15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"}> Cumrun Vafa
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Reflections on F-theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://wwwth.mpp.mpg.de/conf/f-theory15/talks/Vafa.pdf"} pdf
          %p Computational tools:
          %ul
            %li
              Martin Bies, Miķelis E. Miķelsons, Andrew P. Turner:
              %em FTheoryTools: Advancing Computational Capabilities for F-Theory Research
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.13849"}> arXiv:2506.13849
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Related conferences:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://www.match.uni-heidelberg.de/GPF/"} Physics and Geometry of F-theory 2014
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://f-theory15.mpp.mpg.de"} Physics and Geometry of F‑theory 2015
          %h3#relation_to_orientifolds Relation to orientifolds
          %p
            F-theory lifts of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifold"} orientifold
            backgrounds were first identified in
          %ul
            %li#Sen96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em F-theory and Orientifolds
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9605150"} arXiv:hep-th/9605150
            %li#Sen97a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Orientifold Limit of F-theory Vacua
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9702165"} arXiv:hep-th/9702165
          %p
            and the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+enhancement"} gauge enhancement
            in
          %ul
            %li#Sen97b
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Note on Enhanced Gauge Symmetries in M- and String Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9707123"} arXiv:hep-th/9707123
          %p with more details including
          %ul
            %li
              Zurab Kakushadze,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gary+Shiu"} Gary Shiu
              = succeed "," do
                %em Type IIB Orientifolds, F-theory, Type I Strings on Orbifolds and Type I - Heterotic Duality
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9804092"} arXiv:hep-th/9804092
          %p This is further expanded on in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Elliptic curves in gauge theory, string theory, and cohomology
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0511087"} arXiv:hep-th/0511087
          %h3#relation_to_elliptic_cohomology Relation to elliptic cohomology
          %p
            A series of articles arguing for a relation between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptic fibration
            of F-theory and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology"} elliptic cohomology
            (see also at
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+equivariant+elliptic+cohomology"} modular equivariant elliptic cohomology
          %ul
            %li#KrizSati05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Kriz"}> Igor Kriz
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %em Type II string theory and modularity
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0501060"} arXiv:hep-th/0501060
          %h3#relation_to_heterotic_string_string_theory Relation to heterotic string string theory
          %ul
            %li#FriedmanMorganWitten97
              %p
                Robert Friedman,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Morgan"} John Morgan
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
                %em Vector Bundles And F Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9701162"}> arXiv:hep-th/9701162
                )
            %li#Donagi98
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ron+Donagi"}> Ron Donagi
                ,
                %em ICMP lecture on heterotic/F-theory duality
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9802093"}> arXiv:hep-th/9802093
                )
          %h3#relation_to_mtheory_on_manifolds_2
            Relation to M-theory on
            = succeed "-manifolds" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
          %ul
            %li#GukovYauZaslow02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergei+Gukov"}> Sergei Gukov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shing-Tung+Yau"} Shing-Tung Yau
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Zaslow"} Eric Zaslow
                %em
                  Duality and Fibrations on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
                  Manifolds
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0203217"}> arXiv:hep-th/0203217
                )
            %li#Belhaj02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adil+Belhaj"}> Adil Belhaj
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    F-theory Duals of M-theory on
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi G
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
                    Manifolds from Mirror Symmetry
                %strong 36
                (2003) 4191-4206 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0207208"}> arXiv:hep-th/0207208
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/0305-4470/36/14/319"} doi:10.1088/0305-4470/36/14/319
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mariana+Gra%C3%B1a"}> Mariana Graña
                , C. S. Shahbazi,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Zambon"} Marco Zambon
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Spin
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 7
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(7)
                    \-manifolds in compactifications to four dimensions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1405.3698"} arXiv:1405.3698
          %h3#relation_to_the_6d_superconformal_theory Relation to the 6d superconformal theory
          %p
            Realization to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/6d+%282%2C0%29-supersymmetric+QFT"} 6d (2,0)-supersymmetric QFT
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#HeckmannMorrisonVafa13
              Jonathan Heckman,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Morrison"} David Morrison
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
              %em On the Classification of 6D SCFTs and Generalized ADE Orbifolds
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1312.5746"}> arXiv:1312.5746
              )
          %h3#ReferencesPhenomnenology Phenomenology and model building
          %p
            A large body of literature is concerned with particle physics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+phenomenology"} string phenomenology
            modeled in the context of F-theory, in particular
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GUTs"} GUTs
          %ul
            %li#Denef08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frederik+Denef"}> Frederik Denef
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Les Houches Lectures on Constructing String Vacua
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+theory+and+the+real+world"} String theory and the real world
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0803.1194"}> arXiv:0803.1194
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/780946"} spire:780946
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Beasley"}> Chris Beasley
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Heckman"} Jonathan Heckman
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
                = succeed "," do
                  %em GUTs and Exceptional Branes in F-theory - I
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0802.3391"} arXiv:0802.3391
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Beasley"}> Chris Beasley
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Heckman"} Jonathan Heckman
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
                %em GUTs and Exceptional Branes in F-theory - I
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0802.3391"}> arxiv:0802.3391
                ),
                %em II: Experimental Predictions
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0806.0102"}> arxiv:0806.0102
                )
            %li#Wijhnholt14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Wijnholt"}> Martin Wijnholt
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em String compactification
                %a{:href => "https://pitp2014.ias.edu"} PITP 2014
                lecture notes (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/WijnholtCompactification14.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://static.ias.edu/pitp/2014/sites/pitp2014.ias.edu/files/PITP2014_P1_wijnholt.pdf"} slides for lecture 1
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://static.ias.edu/pitp/2014/sites/pitp2014.ias.edu/files/PITP2014_P2_wijnholt.pdf"} slides for lecture 2
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://static.ias.edu/pitp/2014/sites/pitp2014.ias.edu/files/PITP2014_P3_wijnholt.pdf"} slides for lecture 3
            %li#Zoccarato14
              %p
                Gianluca Zoccarato,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Yukawa couplings at the point of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi E
                            %mn 8
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_8
                    in F-theory
                = succeed "/zoccarato.pdf))" do
                  %a{:href => "http://stringpheno2014.ictp.it/parallels/tuesday/F-theory(B"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion of the
            %em exact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 6
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = \big( SU(3) \times SU(2) \times U(1)\big)/\mathbb{Z}_6
            including its
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 6
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_6
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+group"} quotient
            (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "standard+model+of+particle+physics#GaugeGroup"} there
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermion"} fermion
            field content, realized in F-theory is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Denis Klevers, Damian Kaloni Mayorga Pena, Paul-Konstantin Oehlmann, Hernan Piragua, Jonas Reuter,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em F-Theory on all Toric Hypersurface Fibrations and its Higgs Branches
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1408.4808"} arXiv:1408.4808
            %li#CveticLin17
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mirjam+Cvetic"}> Mirjam Cvetic
                , Ling Lin, section 3.3 of
                %em
                  The global gauge group structure of F-theory compactifications with
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.08521"}> arXiv:1706.08521
                )
          %p
            Based on this large number of realizations of the exact field content of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            (or rather
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSSM"} MSSM
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
            is claimed to be realized in
          %ul
            %li#CveticHalversonLinLiuTian19
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mirjam+Cvetic"}> Mirjam Cvetic
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Halverson"} James Halverson
                %em A Quadrillion Standard Models from F-theory
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.00009"}> arXiv:1903.00009
                )
            %li#TaylorTurner19
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Washington+Taylor"}> Washington Taylor
                , Andrew P. Turner,
                %em Generic construction of the Standard Model gauge group and matter representations in F-theory
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1906.11092"}> arXiv:1906.11092
                )
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fernando+Marchesano"}> Fernando Marchesano
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bert+Schellekens"} Bert Schellekens
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Timo+Weigand"} Timo Weigand
              = succeed "," do
                %em D-brane and F-theory Model Building
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Quantum+Gravity"} Handbook of Quantum Gravity
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.07443"} arXiv:2212.07443
          %p
            Realization of
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E7"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mn 7
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_7
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GUT"} GUT
            models in F-theory:
          %ul
            %li
              Shing Yan Li,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Washington+Taylor"} Washington Taylor
              %em
                Towards natural and realistic
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mn 7
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_7
                GUTs in F-theory
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.00040"}> arXiv:2401.00040
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h4#cosmological_constant Cosmological constant
          %p
            An argument for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+effect"} non-perturbative
            non-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetric
            4d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+phenomenology"} string phenomenology
            with fundamentally vanishing
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmological+constant"} cosmological constant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+8-manifolds"} M-theory on 8-manifolds
            decompactified at strong coupling to 4d via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+M-theory+and+type+IIA+string+theory"} duality between M-theory and type IIA string theory
            (recall the
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+2-brane+in+4d"} super 2-brane in 4d
          %ul
            %li#Witten00
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Cosmological Constant From The Viewpoint Of String Theory
                %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/972507"} DM2000
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0002297"}> arXiv:hep-ph/0002297
                )
              %p (see p. 7)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Strong coupling and the cosmological constant
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9506101"} arXiv:hep-th/9506101
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                , Section 3 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Some Comments On String Dynamics
                %a{:href => "https://cds.cern.ch/record/305869"} Strings95
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9507121"}> arXiv:hep-th/9507121
                )
          %p
            The realization of this scenario in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"}> Cumrun Vafa
                , Section 4.3 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Evidence for F-Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9602022"} arxiv:hep-th/9602022
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Heckman"}> Jonathan Heckman
                , Craig Lawrie, Ling Lin, Gianluca Zoccarato,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em F-theory and Dark Energy
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1811.01959"} arXiv:1811.01959
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1002/prop.201900057"} doi:10.1002/prop.201900057
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Heckman"}> Jonathan Heckman
                , Craig Lawrie, Ling Lin, Jeremy Sakstein, Gianluca Zoccarato,
                %em Pixelated Dark Energy
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1901.10489"}> arXiv:1901.10489
                )
          %h4#flavour_anomalies Flavour anomalies
          %p
            Realization in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
            of
            = succeed "-models" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GUT"} GUT
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Z%27-bosons"} Z'-bosons
            and/or [leptoquarks]] addressing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+anomalies"} flavour anomalies
            and the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "anomalous+magnetic+moment#Anomalies"} (g-2) anomalies
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Miguel Crispim Romao, Stephen F. King, George K. Leontaris,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Non-universal
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Z
                          %mo ′
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z'
                    from Fluxed GUTs
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1710.02349"} arXiv:1710.02349
            %li
              %p
                A. Karozas, G. K. Leontaris, I. Tavellaris, N. D. Vlachos,
                %em
                  On the LHC signatures of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SU
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 5
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ×
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(5) \times U(1)'
                  F-theory motivated models
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2007.05936"}> arXiv:2007.05936
                )
          %h3#FluxAndInstantons 4-Form flux and instantons
          %p
            The image of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            to F-theory yields the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mn 4
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_4
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+compactification"} flux
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Andres Collinucci, Raffaele Savelli,
                %em On Flux Quantization in F-Theory
                (2010) (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1011.6388"}> arXiv:1011.6388
                )
            %li
              %p
                Sven Krause, Christoph Mayrhofer,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Timo+Weigand"} Timo Weigand
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 4
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_4
                  flux, chiral matter and singularity resolution in F-theory compactifications
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1109.3454"}> arXiv:1109.3454
                )
            %li#GKP12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Grimm"}> Thomas Grimm
                , Denis Klevers, Maximilian Poretschkin,
                %em Fluxes and Warping for Gauge Couplings in F-theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1202.0285"}> arXiv:1202.0285
                )
            %li#KMW12
              %p
                Sven Krause, Christoph Mayrhofer,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Timo+Weigand"} Timo Weigand
                %em Gauge Fluxes in F-theory and Type IIB Orientifolds
                (2012) (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1202.3138"}> arXiv:1202.3138
                )
          %p
            and with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instanton"} instanton
            contributions:
          %ul
            %li
              Max Kerstan,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Timo+Weigand"} Timo Weigand
              %em Fluxed M5-instantons in F-theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1205.4720"}> arXiv:1205.4720
              )
          %p Reviewed in
          %ul
            %li#Weigand12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Timo+Weigand"}> Timo Weigand
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Fluxes and M5-instantons in F-theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://people.physik.hu-berlin.de/~ahoop/weigand.pdf"} pdf slides
          %p
            For more on this see also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F%2FM-theory+on+elliptically+fibered+Calabi-Yau+4-folds"} F/M-theory on elliptically fibered Calabi-Yau 4-folds
